# Softogram project rules

Marketing site for Softogram (software dev company).
Tagline: "Your idea. Our code. Delivered."

## Stack

- Frontend: React 19 + JS/JSX, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion, CRACO (`frontend/`)
- Backend: FastAPI + SendGrid (`backend/server.py`)
- Nearly all UI is in `frontend/src/App.js` — extend in place unless asked to refactor

## Brand (do not drift)

- Dark glassmorphism, cyan `#00F5FF`, violet `#7C3AED`, black backgrounds
- Space Grotesk headings, Inter body, Lucide icons
- Glass cards: `bg-white/5 border border-white/10 backdrop-blur-md`
- Add `data-testid` on new interactive elements

## Contact flow

`POST /api/contact` → background SendGrid email.
Budget is appended to `message` on the client.
MongoDB lead save is disabled.

## Constraints

- Minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors of `App.js`
- No TypeScript/Next.js without explicit approval
- Canonical email in code: `support@softogram.com`
- Ignore `.cursor/skills/`, `.claude/skills/` for app changes
- Use `graphify query` for codebase questions when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists
